# RFC 7323 / RFC 5961: a segment dropped for its ACK (here: an ACK of data
# never sent) must not update ts_recent -- else the peer's next, legitimate
# segment fails PAWS and the connection stalls.
# Copyright (C) 2026 The LikeOS Project
0.000 socket s stream
0.000 bind s 8080
0.000 listen s 16
0.100 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
0.100 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
0.200 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 200 ecr echo>
0.200 accept s c
0.300 < P. 1:11(10) ack 5000 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 2000000000 ecr echo>
0.300 > . 1:1(0) ack 1 win * <nop,nop,TS val * ecr 200>
1.000 < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 1000 ecr echo>
1.000 > . 1:1(0) ack 11 win * <nop,nop,TS val * ecr 1000>
1.100 recv c 10 = 10
